cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its benchmark/control results, please cite it as below."
title: "yarvpilled: an A-Life world where every brain is a live YARV instruction sequence"
type: software
authors:
  - alias: "0thernes"
    email: "0_0@0thernes.art"
version: "0.2.0"
date-released: "2026-11-22"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/0thernes/yarvpilled"
url: "https://github.com/0thernes/yarvpilled"
abstract: >-
  A zero-model artificial-life simulation in CRuby. Each creature's brain is a Ruby method
  compiled with RubyVM::InstructionSequence and executed by YARV; genomes mutate on
  reproduction, and selection hot-swaps live methods via TracePoint. The world loop has
  bit-identical pure-Ruby, C, Rust and hand-written x86-64 assembly backends, with a
  repeated-run benchmark and a selection-vs-random-drift control experiment.
keywords:
  - ruby
  - yarv
  - artificial-life
  - genetic-programming
  - yjit
  - c-extension
  - rust
  - assembly
